C++ TEMPLATES - QUICK INTERVIEW NOTES
=========================================================

What are Templates?
-------------------
Templates enable Generic Programming by writing one function/class that works
with multiple data types.

Advantages
----------
✓ Code Reusability
✓ Compile-time Polymorphism
✓ Type Safety
✓ No Code Duplication

Templates are compile-time constructs.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example

template<typename T>
T max(T a, T b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

Compiler Instantiation

max(10,20);      -> max(int,int)

max(2.5,3.5);    -> max(double,double)

The compiler generates functions/classes only when they are used.
This process is called Template Instantiation.

