=========================================================
FUNCTION TEMPLATES
=========================================================

Definition
----------
A single function that works for multiple data types.

Syntax

template<typename T>
T add(T a, T b)
{
    return a + b;
}

---------------------------------------------------------

Type Deduction

Compiler automatically deduces template arguments.

add(10,20);        // T = int

add(2.5,3.5);      // T = double

---------------------------------------------------------

Multiple Template Parameters

template<typename T, typename U>
auto add(T a, U b)
{
    return a + b;
}

---------------------------------------------------------

Explicit Template Arguments

add<int>(10,20);

Used when type deduction fails.

---------------------------------------------------------

typename vs class

template<typename T>

template<class T>

Both are identical.

---------------------------------------------------------

Normal Function vs Template

void print(int);

template<typename T>
void print(T);

print(10);      // Normal function

print(2.5);     // Template

Rule:
Non-template function is preferred if both match equally well.

---------------------------------------------------------

Important Interview Points

✓ Generic programming
✓ Compile-time feature
✓ Compiler performs template instantiation
✓ Compiler usually deduces template arguments
✓ Supports multiple template parameters
✓ Templates are generally implemented in header (.h/.hpp) files

